  "name": "abcdeez2",
  "description": "A high-fidelity cognitive modeling framework designed for adaptive training of graph-structured knowledge domains. The system leverages Bayesian parameter estimation and Expected Information Gain (EIG) to optimize task selection, while utilizing Ex-Gaussian response time distributions to detect strategy transitions from serial scanning to direct indexing. Its architecture supports complex topologies—including cycles, DAGs, and general graphs—integrated within a cross-platform Rust ecosystem featuring a web-backend for longitudinal studies and Xilem-based interactive interfaces.",
